  "note": "Triennial election of the 19 electoral divisions of Dungannon rural district, one member each, polled on 5 June 1952. Twelve Unionists and five Nationalists were returned unopposed; Crossdernott and Coalisland were contested. The new council had thirteen Unionists and six Nationalists, with three members to be co-opted. M'Ivor was the outgoing member."
